  volume = 94,
  number = 18,
  pages = {7001-7},
  abstract = {C/sub 5/H/sub 3//sup +/ isomeric structures are identified and
             characterized according to their vibrational and electronic
             spectra for possible identification in sooting flame environments
             and in model FT-ICR experiments. By using quantum chemical means,
             it is found that the cyclopropenylium cation is the most stable
             species (MP2/6-31G*//6-31G*), more stable than the others
             investigated by at least 20 kcal/mol. An estimate of 375 kcal/mol
