             conjunction with various seemingly conflicting experimental and
             theoretical results is made. The UV visible spectra is computed
             assuming each of five possible ground states, /sup 1/A/sub 1g/,
             /sup 3/A/sub 2g/, /sup 3/E/sub g/, /sup 5/E/sub g/, /sup 5/A/sub
             1g/, and /sup 5/E/sub g/. The calculated spectra from the /sup
             3/A/sub 2g/ and /sup 3/E/sub g/ states are in good accord with
             experiment, and the authors argue that the extra bands observed
             at 12500 and 15000 cm/sup -1/ are due to trip-triplets, porphyrin
             pi to pi * triplets that have gained intensity by spin coupling
             with the iron atom triplet state. The calculated charge-transfer
             and d to d spectra are described and are compared with other
             calculations. Although d to d states are predicted to lie below
